## §4 Result model & combat log

Move resolution writes three independent, optional result fields on the fight
story. For example, a missed attack can also trigger a counter. The log copies
these fields into each entry and supplies a utility outcome when none was set.

| Fight var | Entry mirror | Values | Meaning |
|---|---|---|---|
| `pod_combat_last_outcome` | `entry.var:outcome` | Fight: `flag:attack` / `heal` / `morale_damage` / `morale_healed`, or absent. Entry: the same plus `utility` | What kind of action the row was; `push_log` supplies `utility` only on the entry when the fight outcome is absent. |
| `pod_combat_last_attack_result` | `entry.var:attack_result` | `flag:hp_damage` / `soaked` / `immune` / `missed` / `dodged` / `stealthed` / `guard_blocked` | How the attack resolved. **Meaningful only when `outcome = flag:attack`** — readers gate on the outcome axis first. |
| `pod_combat_last_retal_fired` | `entry.var:retal_fired` | `1` or absent | Overlay: a counter-strike resolved. Independent of the other two. |

`PODCombatLogResultText` renders the entry's outcome and attack result;
`PODCombatLogRetalRider` renders its counter. `stealthed` and `dodged` both
auto-miss but link to different concepts. `immune` and `soaked` both cause zero
HP damage, but immunity belongs to neither the contact nor miss partition.

**Damage classification and soak are recorded per packet.** PoD's per-victim
classification determines the wound-box icon (see **Damage pipeline**):

- `pod_combat_last_result_agg` is the aggregate marker.
- `pod_combat_last_primary_result_agg` → `entry.var:result_agg` records the
  main packet; `pod_combat_last_typed_bonus_result_agg_<k>` →
  `entry.var:typed_bonus_result_agg_<k>` records each typed packet.
- `pod_combat_last_retal_agg` / `_last_retal_morale` →
  `entry.var:retal_agg` / `retal_morale` classifies the counter.

An absent aggravated marker means superficial only after a positive-damage
branch. Miss, immunity, full soak, and zero-damage counters have separate branches.

`pod_combat_last_soaked_count` remains an aggregate fallback. The main packet's
`pod_combat_last_primary_soaked_count` → `entry.var:soaked_count` and each
`pod_combat_last_typed_bonus_soaked_count_<k>` →
`entry.var:typed_bonus_soaked_count_<k>` select their partial-soak lines.
The counter displays post-soak damage without a separate absorbed count.

### How scripted effects write the axes

- **Miss / dodge / stealth / guard:**
  `pod_combat_set_attack_result_effect = { CODE = ... }` writes
  `outcome = flag:attack` and `attack_result = flag:$CODE$` together.
  Damage routing supplies `scope:attack_result_flag` (`hp_damage` / `soaked` /
  `immune`) to `pod_combat_apply_damage_payload_effect`. The primary and typed
  scripted effects copy the packet result into their log snapshots.
- **HP heal / morale damage / morale heal:**
  `pod_combat_set_outcome_if_unset_effect = { CODE = ... }` preserves an existing
  outcome. A damage+heal move keeps `attack`; `pod_combat_last_heal_amount`
  supplies its heal rider.
- **Retaliation:** `pod_combat_set_retal_fired_effect` sets the counter field
  without changing either other result field.

### Reset, sentinel, and the utility default

§2 of `POD_execute_combat_move` calls
`pod_combat_clear_last_result_vars_effect` to remove all three result fields,
aggregate results, and packet snapshots. **Absence means no result yet.**
At log push, an absent fight outcome becomes `entry.var:outcome = flag:utility`
(for example, a pure stance). Unset `attack_result` and `retal_fired` stay absent.

Practice mode uses the ordinary contact, damage, Morale-spillover,
retaliation, and logging paths while the spar is live. At combat end it
restores each pre-fight wound snapshot and skips Morale-to-Mental-Strain
conversion. Persistent effects are not handled uniformly: Gold theft,
Dread gains, target Energy drains, and wound side effects are
suppressed; conditional actor Energy gains still apply, and listed move
costs remain paid.
See **Combat end** for the full cleanup contract.

### Result-code partition triggers

`pod_combat_move_execution_triggers.txt` groups attack results for riders and
reactions. The gates require `outcome = flag:attack`, except that the HP-damage
gate also accepts the AoE latch described below.

| Trigger | Passes on |
|---|---|
| `pod_combat_result_code_indicates_hp_damage_trigger` | `attack_result = hp_damage` — a wound went through. (OR'd with the `pod_combat_aoe_any_hp_damage` latch so an AoE drain heals once if **any** target took HP damage, since the per-target log clear wipes the fight axes mid-loop.) |
| `pod_combat_result_code_indicates_contact_trigger` | `attack_result` ∈ (`hp_damage`, `guard_blocked`, `soaked`) — anything that physically touched, even if absorbed. Used by retaliate-on-contact and `on_contact` riders. |
| `pod_combat_result_code_indicates_miss_trigger` | `attack_result` ∈ (`missed`, `dodged`, `stealthed`) — the attack was evaded. Used by retaliate-on-evasion and `on_miss` riders. |
| `pod_combat_result_code_indicates_attack_trigger` | any `attack_result` at all. **Not a partition member** — the union of the whole axis, so `immune` (which belongs to neither of the two above) and any future code qualify. Used by retaliate-on-any-attack, via the scripted trigger `pod_combat_reaction_any_condition_trigger`. |

### Combat log

The combat log records resolved actions and system messages. Each row is a `POD_combat_log_entry` story owned by Charon
(`character:POD_wraith_01`, a guaranteed-alive anchor); the fight story's
`pod_combat_log` variable list holds references to them, and its
`pod_combat_log_seq` counter numbers them.

#### Append-only, capped at 30

`pod_combat_append_capped_log_entry_effect` appends action and system entries
to `pod_combat_log`, stamps `log_seq`, and ends the oldest story when the list
exceeds `pod_combat_log_max_entries` (30). It finds that entry by lowest
`log_seq` with `ordered_in_list`.

The GUI `vbox` uses **`bottomtotop`** to show this oldest-first list newest-first.
Keep that display order: variable lists append and GUI datamodels cannot sort.
`log_seq` is used only for trimming.

Two callers create the entries:

- **`pod_combat_push_log_effect`** — the per-action row. Snapshots one
  resolved move: a live `move` story reference (the GUI reads the damage
  class, targeting, and the primitive flags off it), `actor` /
  `target` char refs, `actor_side`, optional `aoe_burst_index`, the
  amount fields (`damage`, `typed_bonus_damage_<k>`, `heal_amount`,
  `morale_damage_amount`, `morale_heal_amount`, `self_damage`,
  `retal_damage`, `energy_gain`, `energy_drain`, `ap_refund`,
  `soaked_count`, `typed_bonus_soaked_count_<k>`), the
  three result-axis vars (`outcome` /
  `attack_result` / `retal_fired`, see **Result model**), the
  actual-result markers (`result_agg` / `typed_bonus_result_agg_<k>` /
  `retal_agg` / `retal_morale`), each typed packet's
  `typed_bonus_attack_result_<k>` / `typed_bonus_damage_class_<k>`,
  and the segment-visibility bake described below. The typed fields exist
  for `k` = 1..3. Each captured packet writes `typed_bonus_attack_result_<k>`
  alongside its damage, class, and soak count; testing for that result variable
  guards all fields in the packet.
- **`pod_combat_push_system_log_effect`** (and the `_named` sibling,
  which also stamps `actor`) — a move-less row carrying only a
  `system_message` flag.

#### The result column

The result column consists of a primary result followed by segments separated
with ` · `.

- **`PODCombatLogResultText`** reads `entry.var:outcome` and
  `entry.var:attack_result`, with `result_agg` selecting the wound-box icon.
  It covers hit / soaked / immune / blocked / missed / dodged / stealthed,
  heal / morale-damage / morale-heal / utility.
- **`PODCombatLogSeg*`** render the independent segments below.

| Segment | Renders when the move has |
|---------|--------------------------|
| `PODCombatLogSegTypedBonusDamage1` / `2` / `3` | a typed conditional-damage packet was routed into that slot; each shows its own landed/soaked/immune result, actual wound box, amount, absorbed count and authored class. Three customizable localization definitions are needed because customizable localization takes no parameters and `PODSegText` can only vary the definition name |
| `PODCombatLogSegRecoil` | self-damage > 0 on the entry |
| `PODCombatLogSegHitTier` | a hit buff/debuff tier |
| `PODCombatLogSegSoakTier` | a soak buff/debuff tier |
| `PODCombatLogSegGuard` | `set_guard` |
| `PODCombatLogSegDodge` | `dodge` |
| `PODCombatLogSegStealth` | `stealth` |
| `PODCombatLogSegRemoveGuard` | `remove_guard` |
| `PODCombatLogSegRetalArmed` | `retaliate_if_hit` / `retaliate_if_missed` / `retaliate_if_attacked` |
| `PODCombatLogSegApGain` | `ap_gain` |
| `PODCombatLogSegApDrain` | a drain that applied (`ap_drain` > 0 on the entry — the base plus a fired `ap_drain` bonus; a drain reaching `pod_combat_base_ap` renders as 0 AP next turn) |
| `PODCombatLogSegInitDebuff` | `initiative_debuff` |
| `PODCombatLogSegEnergyGain` | an energy restore that applied: the `energy_gain` column and/or a fired bonus (`energy_gain` > 0 on the entry) |
| `PODCombatLogSegEnergyDrain` | a fired `energy_drain` bonus (`energy_drain` > 0 on the entry) |
| `PODCombatLogSegApRefund` | a fired `ap_refund` bonus (`ap_refund` > 0 on the entry) |
| `PODCombatLogSegMarker` | `marker_modifier` (the marker this move applied to its user) |

Separate **amount riders** (`PODCombatLogHealRider`,
`PODCombatLogMoraleDamageRider`, `PODCombatLogMoraleHealRider`,
`PODCombatLogRetalRider`) append the actual numbers for heal / morale /
counter effects that ride alongside the primary line. The retal rider
splits positive damage on the entry's `retal_morale` / `retal_agg`
markers (morale / aggravated / superficial) and renders a zero-damage
fired counter as soaked. It displays the post-soak counter magnitude;
there is no separate absorbed-count split.

#### Visibility is baked once at push time

`pod_combat_push_log_effect` records segment visibility after the amounts and
results, in display order. Each visible segment gets two presence variables:

- `seg_<x>_on`: render the segment.
- `seg_<x>_sep`: prepend ` · ` if the head or an earlier segment has content.

`seg_bake_prior` counts preceding content. The head counts unless its outcome
is `utility`, whose text is empty. The visibility values in
`pod_combat_values.txt` (`pod_combat_log_seg_<x>_visible_value`,
`pod_combat_log_before_<x>_value`, and `*_rider_visible_value`) read these
immutable entry variables.

The bake conditions:

- **Typed bonus damage** (three, baked in slot order before every other
  segment): that slot's packet result was captured. This is per-target outcome
  data and is never AoE burst-gated. A typed row is always `outcome = attack`,
  so `seg_bake_prior` starts at 1 and slot 1 always draws its separator.
- **Heal / morale riders**: amount captured and `> 0`, `NAND` outcome
  equals the rider's own primary (so a pure-heal row doesn't
  double-print the heal). `NAND`, not `NOT` — `outcome` is always
  stamped, so a multi-child `NOT` (= `NOR`) would be permanently false
  and silently kill the rider.
- **Retal rider**: `retal_fired` present.
- **Move-level segments:** `pod_combat_log_seg_burst_gate_trigger` admits only
  non-AoE rows or the first burst row (`aoe_burst_index = 0`). This prevents
  repeating the same move property for every target.
- **Recoil:** not burst-gated; actor self-damage occurs once and appears on the
  single-target or AoE wrap-up row.
- **Energy, AP refund, and AP drain:** not burst-gated. Their amounts are
  captured only when applied and cleared per push. Energy gain/drain is captured
  at §9b (drain inside the practice gate), AP refund/drain at §14. The AP-drain
  capture also sits inside the control-failure guard, so resisted control does
  not log a drain. Using the applied total lets bonus-only drains render and
  identifies a base+bonus stack that removes all next-turn AP.
- **Marker:** burst-gated; it reads the move's `marker_modifier`, which §12c
  applies unconditionally.

Rows that skip the bake (system / DoT / mind / daze rows) carry no
`seg_*` vars and read as all-invisible.

**Widget order in `pod_combat_window.gui` must match the visibility order in
`pod_combat_push_log_effect`.** Every recorded segment needs its widget pair.
Separators are determined before rendering; reordered or missing widgets can
leave misplaced or leading ` · ` separators.

#### System and bookend rows

Move-less rows carry a flag-valued `system_message` and render via
`PODCombatLogSystemMessageText`. Lifecycle bookends:

| `system_message` | Pushed when |
|------------------|-------------|
| `combat_started` | combat begins |
| `round_begins` | each new round |
| `combat_ended_victory` / `combat_ended_defeat` | combat ends (which side won) |
| `combatant_joins` | a mid-fight summon seats a combatant (named row) |
| `ally_down_shock` | a teammate is knocked out (named row) |
| `form_shifted` | a combatant changes shape mid-fight (named row) |
| `delirium_struck` | PoD's Delirium lands on a combatant (named row, once per victim per fight) |

The same customizable localization also handles DoT (`dot_applied_*` / `dot_tick_*`),
daze/stun (`dazed` / `stunned`), and mind-control (`mind_seized` /
`mind_resisted` / `mind_betrayal` / `mind_fizzle`) rows, each pushed by
its own scripted effect (`pod_combat_push_dot_applied_log_effect`,
`pod_combat_push_dot_tick_log_effect`,
`pod_combat_push_ap_drain_log_effect`,
`pod_combat_push_mind_log_effect`). All set `actor_side = -1` so the GUI
renders them in the neutral system lane.

#### AoE rows

An AoE move pushes one row per target. `target` names the iterated character
(e.g. "All enemies (Steve)" or "Everyone (Steve)"), and `aoe_burst_index`
starts at 0 for the move-level segment gate.

The iterator sets `pod_combat_aoe_phase_pushed_rows`. This suppresses the final
wrap-up row unless it still has actor-side results to report:
`pod_combat_last_heal_amount`, `pod_combat_last_morale_heal_amount`,
`pod_combat_last_retal_fired`, `pod_combat_last_self_damage`,
`pod_combat_last_energy_gain` / `_drain`, or
`pod_combat_last_ap_refund` / `_last_ap_drain`. That row carries those remaining
riders. Non-AoE moves leave the flag unset and push one row.

